# Data, weights, and simulator output stay out of git
data/
datasets/
checkpoints/
# ...except the two students the published certificate actually loads. 403 KB total:
# without them a clone contains the answer (sustained_bound.json) and nothing that
# produced it. Every other checkpoint (teachers, DAgger rounds, width variants) stays out.
!pipeline/checkpoints/
pipeline/checkpoints/*
# EVERY SHIPPED POLICY, and the final teacher each was distilled from. 5.5 MB in total,
# so there is no reason to make an external researcher reconstruct them -- and with the
# renderer's irreducible per-frame nondeterminism (carla-determinism D-7) a reconstruction
# would not be bit-identical anyway. Training checkpoints (BC, intermediate DAgger rounds,
# width variants) stay out: they are scaffolding, not results.
#
# Town04, published:
!pipeline/checkpoints/S_clear_84x28.pth
!pipeline/checkpoints/S_mixed_84x28_w3.pth
# Town04, redo under the corrected harness (T04-R5; the mixed policy is the
# student-DAgger'd checkpoint, which is what final_student resolves to):
!pipeline/checkpoints/S_clear_84x28_v2.pth
!pipeline/checkpoints/S_mixed_84x28_w3_v2_dagger_r00.pth
# Town06 deployment test:
!pipeline/checkpoints/S_clear_t06_168x28_w2.pth
!pipeline/checkpoints/S_mixed_t06_168x28_w3.pth
# the final teachers, so a student can be re-distilled without re-running DAgger:
!pipeline/checkpoints/teacher_clear_v3_dagger_r05.pth
!pipeline/checkpoints/teacher_mixed_v2_dagger_r03.pth
!pipeline/checkpoints/teacher_clear_t06_dagger_r06.pth
!pipeline/checkpoints/teacher_mixed_t06_dagger_r11.pth
# ...and the Town06 deployment-test routes. These are PROTOCOL artifacts, not data:
# the route had to be fixed, on geometry alone, before any Town06 model existed, and
# committing it is what makes that checkable later. ~23 KB each.
!pipeline/data/
pipeline/data/*
!pipeline/data/routes_town06/
# ...and the TOWN04 routes, for exactly the same reason. They are the geometric
# definition of the published lap and they were never tracked -- the published artifact
# could not be reproduced from its own repository without them. 52 KB.
!pipeline/data/routes/
runs/
results/**/*.png
results/**/*.npy
# .npz captures are simulator output: 18 GB of them, regenerable from the scripts.
# The .npy rule above did not cover the compressed archives the capture scripts write.
results/**/*.npz
results/traces/
results/**/*.pt
!results/ledger/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv*/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Local notes
scratch/

# trajectory frame logs: ~0.5 GB per lap, regenerable
results/traj/
results/trajectory/*.json

# driven-frame logs (regenerable; 144 MB per run)
results/framelog/

# Town06 deployment test: captures are simulator output (~38 MB x 8) and regenerable.
# The CERTIFICATE is not -- it is the pre-drive prediction and must be committed.
results/town06/captures/
results/town06_logs/
!results/town06/
!results/town06/certificate_town06.json
!results/town06/ledger/
# The PER-RUN artifacts and their step traces. `runs/` above excluded these, so the
# committed Town06 result carried only eight aggregated cells: the three laps behind each
# verdict, their margins, and where each one peaked were all untracked. That is the
# evidence A-4 asks for ("report the margin with every verdict") and R-SIM-6 asks for
# ("check step counts before reading verdicts"), and none of it was in the repository.
#
# The traces also make a cell RE-SCORABLE. Without them a scored span is baked into the
# verdict at drive time, and asking what a different span would have given means driving
# 24 laps again -- which is exactly what it cost to ask that question once.
# ~95 KB per lap, 24 laps per pass.
!results/town06/ledger/runs/
!results/town06/ledger/runs/**
# ...and for every A-5 pass and scope. A pass writes ledger_pass<N>/ and the scope
# scorer writes ledger_<scope>/, and `runs/` above would exclude their per-run artifacts
# exactly as it excluded pass 1's. Spelling only pass 1 here is how the next pass
# silently loses its evidence again.
#
# Only .json and .csv are re-included. A bare `**` would also re-admit the .npz and .png
# rules above, which exist because these directories are where 18 GB of simulator output
# lands -- the re-inclusion must be narrower than the exclusion it is reopening.
!results/town06/ledger_*/
!results/town06/ledger_*/**/
!results/town06/ledger_*/**/*.json
!results/town06/ledger_*/**/*.csv
!results/town06/ledger_*/*.json
!results/town06/ledger_*/*.csv

# Determinism campaign (T06-F22). The SUMMARIES are the result and are committed; the
# per-rep traces and raw frame dumps are bulk evidence, regenerable from the probes in
# scripts/determinism_*.py, and raw frames are large binaries.
results/town06/determinism/*_rep*.json
results/town06/determinism/frames/

# pipeline/results is evaluate.py's SCRATCH directory -- every exploratory run writes a
# per-step CSV and PNG there, and a sweep writes dozens. Only the traces the paper reports
# are tracked. 572 scratch files were committed during the Town06 rebuild and the Town04
# redo before this rule existed; they are archived, not deleted.
pipeline/results/*
!pipeline/results/eval_teacher_clear_bc_*.csv
!pipeline/results/eval_teacher_clear_bc_*.png
!pipeline/results/oracle_*.csv
!pipeline/results/oracle_*.png
!pipeline/results/reference_routes.png
!pipeline/results/teacher_clear_bc_training.png
!pipeline/results/teacher_mixed_bc_training.png

# The gate artifact is EVIDENCE, not bulk data: the captures it describes are
# gigabytes and stay out, but the JSON that says they reproduce the vehicle is the
# record that a stated precondition was actually checked. It must be in git.
!results/town06/captures/capture_gate.json
